                <pb facs="1029" n="909" xml:id="pg909"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2618: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hanson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-25T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Stevens: Your July 22, 4 p.m. received and contents carefully noted.</p>
                <p>Situation is certainly fraught with difficulty but I am convinced that we have
                    adopted the only course possible under the circumstances. Your observations and
                    recommendations are always welcome and I shall keep you advised of
                    developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
